# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever platform checks them out.
# This repo is edited on Windows and the scripts run on Linux (the base station
# Pi, and a tester's laptop). A CRLF checkout copied to Linux fails with
# "\r: command not found" on the shebang line — an error that names neither the
# script nor the real problem.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Firmware images are binary; never let autocrlf near them. A single mangled byte
# is a bricked flash, and the corruption would not show until the timer failed to
# boot.
*.bin binary
